{
  "id": "29400_shizumeru",
  "headword": "{鎮|しず}める",
  "reading": "しずめる",
  "romaji": "shizumeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to quell; to calm; to suppress",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to quell; to calm; to suppress",
      "explanation": "To bring something turbulent under control — a rebellion, a commotion, pain, or one's anger. The transitive partner of {鎮|しず}まる (to subside, to die down)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29400_shizumeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{反乱|はんらん}を{鎮|しず}める。",
      "english": "to quell a rebellion",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29400_shizumeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{薬|くすり}で{痛|いた}みを{鎮|しず}める。",
      "english": "to relieve pain with medicine",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29400_shizumeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{怒|いか}りを{鎮|しず}めようと{深呼吸|しんこきゅう}をした。",
      "english": "He took a deep breath to calm his anger.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: X を {鎮|しず}める (quell X). The intransitive partner is {鎮|しず}まる (to subside, to die down).\n\nUSAGE:\nTypical objects are disturbances and strong feelings: {反乱|はんらん} (rebellion), {騒|さわ}ぎ (commotion), {痛|いた}み (pain), {怒|いか}り (anger).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS (same reading しずめる):\n- {静|しず}める: to quiet (noise, a crowd) — to make calm or quiet\n- {沈|しず}める: to sink (something) — to send under water",
